  "notes": {
    "superstore": "Owner 2026-11-08: the store was a sealed shell (painted doors only). The four painted glass double doors at the front are cut open (y 0-3.2), three loading-dock bays in the back wall (3.6 x 4.2 m), and six personnel doors with door panels: west wall, east wall (2), the notch court's east wall, the back wall by the stockroom, the west strip's front. The fit-out is the procedural superstore-interior model (build_superstore_interior.mjs), whose openings match these.",
    "terminal": "Island Airfield terminal (owner's 2026-11-08 download; owner: new buildings must be enterable with opening doors). The import stands on a 0.9 m floor slab with porches north and south and no way up: steps onto both porches; doors in the north porch doorway (the modelled opening into the hall), the south vestibule's glazing and the east wing's south wall (its own steps); the closet wall behind the north doorway is opened into the hall.",
    "ruined-cabin": "Owner 2026-11-08 (new buildings enterable, with opening doors): the hunters' ruined log cabin in the woods (wildlands) is open at its fallen south end; its side doorway (0.6 m between the logs) is widened to 0.95 m and gets a plank door. The cabin stands with its floor (0.31 m up its foundation logs) at the highest ground under it. The porch's low roof beams (1.8 m over its deck) lose their collision, so the porch can be walked.",
    "landmarks": "Owner 2026-11-08 (new buildings enterable, with opening doors): hospital, school, rail depot, brick switch house and chapel are fitted out by art/br/fitout/landmarks.py (liner walls, ceilings, slabs, stairs, doors)."
  },
